B.boK=new A.df(B.aCl,"\u1e62\u0101d (\u0635) \u2014 It is a heavy letter: the back of the tongue rises towards the roof of the mouth, so the sound is full. Open the Letters school in the Academy and start the lesson for \u1e62\u0101d: you will see the letter, practise it and answer a gentle question. Say its name three times, slowly. Which letter did you learn just before this one?")
B.avg=s(["dad heavy","heavy dad","\u1e0dad","duad","letter \u1e0dad","the \u1e0dad"],t.s)
B.bp3=new A.df(B.avg,"\u1e0c\u0101d (\u0636) \u2014 It is a heavy letter, made with the side of the tongue against the upper molars. Open the Letters school in the Academy and start the lesson for \u1e0c\u0101d: you will see the letter, practise it and answer a gentle question. Say its name three times, slowly. Which letter did you learn just before this one?")
